{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790888589,"nonce":"hC6b/cFzAhp41MLngXDN3WrAx7w=","title":"A Finding carries no Classification, so neither a card nor an external tool can act on what kind of problem it is","message":"**What is wrong.** ADR 0053 §5: a closed, operator-written class set plus `unclassified`; oto ships no classes; a Finding keeps its class if the set changes; classes travel outbound and the docs warn that paging on one is paging on a model's judgement.\n\n**Where.** Org-level class set; Finding field; Slack card; outbound metadata; docs.\n\n**Scope.** small.\n\n**Done when.** With no classes configured, Findings carry no classification; with classes, the model must pick one or `unclassified`; renaming a class does not rewrite old Findings; the docs warning exists.\n\n**Blocked by.** `180a525`\n\n**Mode.** AFK — can be implemented and merged without a human decision. Source: ADR 0052/0053/0054 design session, 2026-10-02.","files":null}]}